  "slug": "association-adjusting-2e22",
  "summary": "New tools and resources tie fine-mapped GWAS signals to cell types and RNA regulatory layers, with T2D as a recurring test case.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving GWAS loci into effector genes and the cellular contexts in which they act. CELL-X carries fine-mapped T2D genes into islet single-cell atlases for beta-cell prioritization, while a multi-layer colocalization of 338 T2D signals with GTEx adipose data extends beyond expression to exon, transcript and splice-junction usage. EPIC2 links GWAS summary statistics to single-cell chromatin accessibility, accounting for LD, to rank trait-relevant cell types. CellColocDB provides coloc.abf colocalization across bulk, sorted-cell and single-cell data, and the IGVF Catalog integrates 657 variant-function datasets as a knowledge graph with APIs and an LLM interface. Upstream methods address phenotype scale (SIQReg) and LD references for admixed cohorts (PRS-LDmix), which affect GWAS and polygenic prediction rather than effector-gene assignment directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
